.DS_Store

# Oracle baselines and other scratch copies of the game. One of these — a 218KB duplicate of
# index.html — got committed once because an `rm -f` ran from the wrong directory and reported success.
.tmp-*

# ⚠️ SAME HAZARD, SECOND NAMING CONVENTION, AND THE PATTERN ABOVE DID NOT COVER IT. Measuring anything
# in this game means serving a modified copy of index.html — a sweepable constant, a runtime hook, a
# build captured off HEAD — and a session that names those `.probe-*` instead of `.tmp-*` writes 500KB+
# duplicates that `.tmp-*` never sees. They were cleaned up by hand every time, which is a habit and not
# a guard: one `git add -A` before the `rm` and a stale copy of the whole game is in history for good.
#   The lesson is not "remember to delete them" — it is that a scratch-file rule keyed to ONE prefix is
# one rename away from being no rule at all. If you invent a third convention, add it here first.
.probe-*
# ...except this one, which is committed on purpose: the recorder's browser-support check, small and
# meant to be opened from a link rather than built.
!.probe-record.html

# Capacitor / npm
node_modules/
www/

# capacitor-assets insists on reading `assets/icon.png` and `assets/logo.png`, both of which are
# byte-identical copies of icons/icon-1024.png (verified by md5). Committing them would put a third
# and fourth copy of the same 433KB master in the repo and, worse, create three places to edit when
# the artwork changes. `npm run icons:ios` rebuilds the directory from the one master and regenerates.
assets/

# Recorded play. Input tapes run ~200KB of JSON per minute of play, and they are measurements rather
# than source — the harness that reads them (.harness/) IS committed.
tapes/

# Commercial planning — the free/paid split, the recommended price, the Steam page timing and the
# revenue expectations. It stays on disk and keeps being written; it is simply not part of the public
# repository. Removed from tracking rather than from history: the rest of the log stays intact, and
# every commit body that mentions it still makes sense.
docs/SCOPE.md

# Capacitor native build output. The ios/ project itself IS committed; these parts are generated.
ios/App/Pods/
ios/App/App/public/
DerivedData/
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/

# ⚠️ NOT IGNORED, ON PURPOSE, AND DO NOT "FIX" IT: `ios/App/App.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` carries
# `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = JZB45AQ78T` on both build configurations, and it has been world-readable since the
# repository went public. It is NOT a credential — a Team ID ships inside every signed iOS app anyone can
# download from the App Store; it identifies the developer account and grants no access to it. Checked
# 2026-08-18: no real signing material is tracked anywhere (`.p12`, `.mobileprovision`, `.key`, `.pem`,
# `.cer` all return zero), and the value is absent from `index.html`, so nothing the web build serves
# carries it.
#   It entered in `a55699e` (2026-08-05), FOUR DAYS BEFORE the repository went public, so no push has
# ever newly exposed it — a claim worth checking before repeating, because it was made and was wrong:
# `git grep -c JZB45AQ78T origin/master -- ios/App/App.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` returns 2, and it is on
# all three pushed branches. Author reviewed and accepted it on 2026-08-18.
#   ⚠️ THE PURGE IS THE EXPENSIVE MOVE AND THE ONLY ONE THAT COULD ACTUALLY HURT. `a55699e` is an
# ancestor of `origin/master`, so rewriting moves the FROZEN NAN-submission tip `631bfbf`, and about 55%
# of PATCHNOTE's resolving commit citations change SHA — 76 of 137 on both branches as of this commit,
# reproduced by two independent extractions. ⚠️ RE-RUN IT RATHER THAN QUOTING IT: the count grows with
# PATCHNOTE, and it moved inside a single afternoon — v2 read 71 of 132 four hours before this note was
# written, and three new entries carried it to 76 of 137. The ratio has held at ~55%; the absolute number
# has not. Recipe, because a figure without one is not evidence, and this one went stale while being
# written into a paragraph about reproducible figures:
#     BT=$(printf '\x60'); for h in $(grep -o "${BT}[0-9a-f]\{7,40\}${BT}" docs/PATCHNOTE.md \
#       | tr -d "${BT}" | sort -u); do git rev-parse --verify -q "$h^{commit}" >/dev/null \
#       && git merge-base --is-ancestor a55699e "$h" && echo "$h"; done | wc -l
# All three branches are pushed, so a purge means force-pushing public history. Same call as SCOPE.md
# above and for the same reason: accepted, not purged.
#   ⚠️ AND MOVING IT TO AN xcconfig DOES NOT WORK HERE, which is the repair everyone reaches for first.
# `CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic`, so Xcode writes `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` back into the pbxproj on the next GUI
# build; and `baseConfigurationReference` belongs to CocoaPods on both configurations, which `npm run
# sync` regenerates via `pod install`. The change greps clean and is overridden in practice — the same
# shape as the inline `top`/`right` that `b33d7d3` had to delete for exactly this reason. If you try it
# anyway, verify by REOPENING Xcode and re-grepping the pbxproj, not by reading the diff.

# The key art's SOURCE candidates — several MB of generated PNGs kept for reference while choosing.
# The SHIPPED art is art/*.webp and those ARE tracked; this is the cutting-room floor. Ignored rather
# than deleted because re-deriving a crop or a colour correction needs the original, and regenerating
# it is not reproducible — the prompt is in art/KEYART-BRIEF.md but the seed is gone.
art/candidates/
